<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>K-Line Fast Initialization</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Communication interface for Diagnostics K-Line protocol. Based on the specification: ISO14230-2 "Road vehicles — Diagnostic on K-Line — Part 2: Network and transport layer requirements and services". ISO document date 1997-10-01</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020C55F60' oid='56D9C590FAFE490982D6557823B3CB5F' temploid='187C4DE8D77B423dBD815B30DFD56B55' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>BusType</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Type of transport media</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.BusType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>KLINE</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_00000000053E88C0' oid='82A59EF3449B49a6AADFD6AB356FD6E2' temploid='14B92107F675457e84CA836CC0A2762D' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='10400' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Baudrate</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Represents the desired baud rate. If the desired  baud  rate  cannot  be  achieved  within  the tolerance of the protocol, the interface will remain at the previous baud rate.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_Baudrate</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_00000000053E8560' oid='5DDDBA58D3BA4eb5B3D1D651A8EFA3DF' temploid='C0255583326F49a9BAF42E732191F8D3' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='233' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>EcuAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Physical diagnostic address of the ECU.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_PhysReqTargetAddr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_00000000053E8710' oid='C7ACF374042E4a4bB7B48F16A99E32C6' temploid='0002B39323274072BA918D85D2348D79' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='241' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Using this Addressing Scheme, the Tester Address can not be determined by the ECU during runtime. Therefore the Tester Address has to be fixed.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_TesterSourceAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_00000000053E8A70' oid='00F6EB03AB574c9482932BDDA369EB07' temploid='AE57F466F16C417aBBB7840A72F286DF' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>BroadcastAddress</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the target address for functionally transmitted requests. If this parameter is 0x00, no functional addressing is used.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_FuncReqTargetAddr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_00000000053E8C20' oid='C195809A5076424bA932B26E9F457863' temploid='A0B28E02031C411f8857C50E47B2B71B' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='0' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>HeaderFormatKW</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Header Byte configuration for K-Line protocols (Keyword). 
This setting is used to properly construct the message header bytes to complete the 
PDU. This ComParam is not used if the ComLogicalLink is in RawMode. 
Header bytes are constructed following
 the rules of the protocol specification. This ComParam 
can be used to override any keybyte values received from the ECU during 
initialization.

Value: [0; 8]

0 = Use the header byte format specified by the ECU key bytes
1 = 1 Byte Only (max size = 0x3F)
2 = 2 Bytes (dependent on length)
3 = 2 Bytes always
4 = 3 Bytes Only
5 = 4 Bytes (dependent on length)
6 = 4 Bytes always
7 = OEM-9141 Header Format (ms nibble of first byte = byte count)
8 = No header bytes </TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_HeaderFormatKW</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_00000000053E8DD0' oid='CCCD549AA4E94316A076041C0EE03A96' temploid='B67D4826CD3F48f19D361E4A431C7F09' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='admin' v='2' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>InitializationSettings</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'> Set initialization method.

 1 = 5 Baud Init sequence
 2 = Fast Init sequence
 3 = No Init sequence</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_InitializationSettings</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C61EA0' oid='699011509DAC4aec8914B349026C8E84' temploid='8F8EBFE34C8346edBFFCD9749FA0BE00' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='25' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TIniL</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Sets the duration for the low pulse in a fast initialization sequence.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_TIniL</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C62050' oid='A692756D10D34cb99A4578E8AF2270E4' temploid='42E2E1A5F249407d94CD258A00B77DE9' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='50' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TWup</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Sets total duration of the wakeup pulse (TWUP-TINIL)=high pulse before start communication message.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_TWup</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C62200' oid='CB395B906046444389F3981E220A1D5B' temploid='023E3B7FD2DF4ddc9B514A7DFE6981C0' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='300' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TIdle</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum bus idle time before tester starts the										   address byte sequence or the fast init sequence. </TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_TIdle</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C623B0' oid='E37E597B1624450f9E9A74995575F27E' temploid='F39122CE17CE402a8A109C99CFE6694C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='200' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout in receiving an expected frame after a successful transmit complete. Also used for multiple ECU responses.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_P2Max</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C62560' oid='B3AFA7BAEA7C43e3B6FEA629B6B07B37' temploid='27A9DD12B0AC462e982096A8D41AFB9C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='50' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout in receiving an expected frame after a successful transmit complete. Also used for multiple ECU responses.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_P2Max_Ecu</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C62710' oid='3790B65484B54991A3670A19E02B05FE' temploid='68CE87B07FC9416e9818CA2A19958FF9' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='6000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2ExClient</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enhanced timeout for the client to wait after the reception of a negative response message with response code 78 hex for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_P2Star</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C628C0' oid='F9BA77082EF94a0181C66915C4C6A106' temploid='1DE5739D3C1E4f6bAA9359D8A534F984' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2ExServer</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time  between end of ECU responses and start of new tester request.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_P3Max_Ecu</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C62A70' oid='43512AB745A846b581D4CC94D4DF2B4B' temploid='671EBCE7979E46d99FBAED9AC1C0E0E9' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='55' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3Min</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time between end of non-negative ECU responses and start of new request. The interface will accept all responses up to CP_P3Min time. The interface will allow transmission of a request any time after CP_P3Min. (See CP_RC21RequestTime for minimum time between end of ECU negative responses and start of new requests.)</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_P3Min</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C62C20' oid='3C152562557F41789DA5DED48AD68A02' temploid='E614A852FE5945418DCC9C512C0B08FE' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='0' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P4Min</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum inter-byte time for tester transmits.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_P4Min</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C68EA0' oid='0FB66F4B5D3643b699723968AB20791D' temploid='D351FFDDF82D4e269FE40CAC752C31EC' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='4000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time between functionally addressed Tester Present request messages transmitted by the client to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active in multiple servers (functional communication) or maximum time between physically transmitted request messages to a single server (physical communication).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_TesterPresentTime</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020C69050' oid='66DF003F0E2846ac8975EEA9697FF848' temploid='EB4D6356B62F480d8A7346FDC8B9C89A' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='admin' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for the server to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active while not receiving any diagnostic request message.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>K_Line_FastInitCommonDiagnostics.CP_TesterPresentTime_Ecu</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020C56100' oid='C8424325271E4e209633ED7B12A56488' temploid='A5BD45C6EA5046dc8D5268F8F42A0437' attrcatref='_00000000053B6660' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
