<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for physical requests and responses.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.AddrScheme</QUAL>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Extended</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CACD60' oid='882D78DE03914b63A7B47BD1F10BBC68' temploid='66FB54AF6D6642219C8709A0DCD4A7B6' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for physical requests and responses</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.CanIdType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>29-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CBF550' oid='1ED4260E9CC74ca4857B76543C0007C2' temploid='6FA3169866D745dc8678B7CD88EAE1CB' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1792' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Request CAN-ID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The request CAN identifier for physical requests. The hex value not only describes the identifier but also the priority of the message. The higher the number, the lower the priority. </TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.ReqCanId</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC1BD0' oid='10A0759E4B4D4e25916943EC6DD3B960' temploid='7051DA0A9EEC4f28AE79889C81BF7C6F' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1536' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Response CAN-ID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The response CAN identifier for physical responses.The response for functional requests is sent via the physical path.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.ResCanId</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC1D80' oid='4A3628B87EF846b4A871D1DA33D8CD79' temploid='284C5674185E4d938352BBC435B0F3FE' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>ECU Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Physical diagnostic address of the ECU.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.EcuAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC1F30' oid='CD601E9F24D74f37A90A86F229AEE5E5' temploid='343FD1D5B8674ed5B40F6D451D0FE6C5' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='241' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Tester Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Using this Addressing Scheme, the Tester Address can not be determined by the ECU during runtime. Therefore the Tester Address has to be fixed.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TesterAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CC4BD0' oid='8015B993F1AB408cBB7BDE972047343E' temploid='D26C204699804c089E5D216A39EB735A' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for functional requests.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.AddrSchemeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Extended</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CC4D70' oid='2FBFC53D931F49368149ED3EE3F14C62' temploid='C186F86271094c46AD62612C35EC7F32' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for functional request</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.CanIdTypeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>29-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC20E0' oid='B6904BBAACFD4b04A4B6D3BE70ED507A' temploid='E389B9CBA2A04a8cB689AC13E3914803' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Request CAN-ID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The request CAN identifier for functional requests.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.ReqCanIdFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC2290' oid='11C1EBC92F9A49e59D5D1D58A14E2709' temploid='AE5EBBF687674952B678F5BB1C95EBBE' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='2' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Broadcast Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address of the functional group the ECU belongs to.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.BroadcastAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC2440' oid='54A967BF9C4143ceA2062EA201D1A04E' temploid='8A1296AD633E400192F91A823F3DC85C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='150' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a request message for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.P2Client</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC25F0' oid='5B18058FA8A64e32AF513AF1ADBCCD8F' temploid='3CFD66C96FE34f5f8A048C589A505F36' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the reception of a request message. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.The tester will also require the P2Server timeout, since in UDS service "DiagnosticSessionControl"returns the P2Server and P2*Server timeouts – the tester has to calculate the offset manually and has to add it to the returned P2Server and P2*Server timeouts.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.P2Server</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC27A0' oid='33411B6EB0BB4e4bAC90783AAA626CAC' temploid='254CB6FC5C8A4df189F954E17EB91D8C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='2000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2*Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enhanced timeout for the client to wait after the reception of a negative response message with response code 78 hex for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.P2ExClient</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CC2950' oid='FA75BBFBF6A74650BC6BD299D13D8385' temploid='3376B2ADB8804636B090055779EC31C8' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='1950' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2*Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the transmission of a negative response message with response code 78 hex (enhanced response timing). In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.P2ExServer</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCC2B0' oid='1619D34AF6BE4905AD03DEEA43B8D843' temploid='9162A26EC31D402d9CE517BD3987C623' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='4000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time between functionally addressed Tester Present request messages transmitted by the client to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active in multiple servers (functional communication) or maximum time between physically transmitted request messages to a single server (physical communication).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.S3Client</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCC460' oid='B826FF70CDCD40689CA4B49263B1F11D' temploid='D073ED1AAEEC4b6fA4A8EC50805FF2F1' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for the server to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active while not receiving any diagnostic request message</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.S3Server</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCC610' oid='9D9FBF36639B4f2c924A19014DF0126D' temploid='CFBFA4437246467c85E960080615E6E2' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a physically addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) with no response required before it can transmit the next physically addressed request message.
Minimum value = P2Server</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.P3ClientPhys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCC7C0' oid='7ED52D02297C45e18B94C7CD42822D30' temploid='80B2781EDEC64e40B044707EC09E739D' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='15872' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterPresentPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the TesterPresent message for physically addressed requests used to keep a diagnostic session active.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TesterPresentPhys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCC970' oid='2DB6620610B345749EB922D5AFD40BD6' temploid='1515824EF20541659D81700D138184A7' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a functionally addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) before it can transmit the next functionally addressed request message in case no response is required or the requested data is only supported by a subset of the functionally addressed servers.
Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.P3ClientFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCCB20' oid='5FCFC2E442FC44c09FAB41304C436BFA' temploid='CA3D0EED4A21499284D932D3AAE1A33E' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='16000' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterPresentFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the TesterPresent message for functionally addressed requests used to keep a diagnostic session active.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TesterPresentFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCCCD0' oid='354BA092A04F41c4A35730B0D251E81A' temploid='37D0920040B54a42B9EE8CFA2A724C41' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='20' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>STmin</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(Separation Time) defines the minimum time gap between consecutive frames.Values from 0x00 to 0x7F (0 – 127) are absolute milliseconds.Values from 0xF1 to 0xF9 are even 100 micro seconds.Every other value range is reserved and should not be used.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.StMin</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCCE80' oid='670FA282B65542b49F0B77DAE5472DFD' temploid='9903F95640A34498896D77808EAD8CA6' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Blocksize</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The Blocksize parameter indicates, how many consecutive frames shall be sent in a transmission before a flow control frame is sent. The number 0 tells the sender, that no more flow controls should disrupt the sending of the remaining flow controls</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.Blocksize</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CCD030' oid='9FC2B5F71E064ac1867ED93DA41A8E8F' temploid='76071E5E12AC4816A969EB36889BAB0E' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout As</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for transmission of frame, sender side</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TimeoutAs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD32B0' oid='D873DCE40E7B4de6A4A7B5F97FE544F8' temploid='A379ED69E9D145879989F0B841026193' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Ar</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for transmission of frame, receiver side</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TimeoutAr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD3460' oid='BE30A46014BB4ec0B1D9FD386A6A0482' temploid='70C145A1F1AF423bAD5F2E2A35E00D4B' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Bs</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until reception of next flow control</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TimeoutBs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD3610' oid='C6110E680A9C4321922F3935825A6A55' temploid='75E6355CF10E4d8cA3182A7CDA435ED6' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time Br</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for next transmission of flow control</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TimeBr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD37C0' oid='CC0324F919BB4e189710C4B48ECA3A00' temploid='568967FF70334ac48254213A39307EAA' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time Cs</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until next transmission of consecutive frame</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TimeCs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD3970' oid='4A2E9E9CEC8249b2B4BC4892E3C24775' temploid='35400E457C7F46deA35226E512BCA57F' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Cr</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until reception of next consecutive frame</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.TimeoutCr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD3B20' oid='3F7213A6C5894d63B4E1A74CC242807A' temploid='01008BE61A0D479b85BE9CBDA35698FA' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='4095' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Max Length of TP Message</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.MaxLengthTpMessage</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD3CD0' oid='F3234B222A98480fB151F463AFC4EA22' temploid='1DAD9E0442D14addB15508193F3F942C' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='500000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Baudrate</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Bus Speed of the used transport media. Caution, the Bus Speed has to be set identical in all ECUs connected to one subnet.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.Baudrate</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD3E80' oid='59246E3846BD4107AE7A966B1D8276F3' temploid='DDB02A0B983A4b6191992026BA03D84C' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CANFrameFillerByte</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Fill byte used for filling CAN frames to eight byte length.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Extended_29Bit.CANFrameFillerByte</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
