<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CC5730' oid='E53E5F96B8754dc9A1F7D90492A5E144' temploid='A2E0FBAAB91149baAA780CC1C9FA32B7' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for physical requests and responses</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.CanIdType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CD4030' oid='D428021824F84adaB563F70BA5940428' temploid='595D9385F4554e38811C99B7C6980207' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1792' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Request CAN-ID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The request CAN identifier for physical requests. The hex value not only describes the identifier but also the priority of the message. The higher the number, the lower the priority. </TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.ReqCanId</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDA6B0' oid='7B89A7CA73834eacB1150E913A5D521C' temploid='846C8F7BBA69494594B552F761484133' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1536' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Response CAN-ID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The response CAN identifier for physical responses.The response for functional requests is sent via the physical path.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.ResCanId</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDA860' oid='6F9996A23F7E453a924A239C37E68D0E' temploid='FE5D8BBCB97840398D592732E204B478' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address Extension</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address Extension transmitted with the first data byte of the message frame. The Address Extension usually specifies a different subnet.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.AddressExtension</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CC58D0' oid='D45944F111494c75B29567D13AFA4CA3' temploid='EDA8A7EFA9AA442096175F04480DE2F0' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='3' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for functional requests.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.AddrSchemeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='3'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE36B0' oid='0306F1FEECC945dbB5D2C1AACD3E48ED' temploid='339A4D6385DD4e83931E6DC2B7B07921' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for functional request</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.CanIdTypeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDAA10' oid='0610D7A7BEE34ac38CFF380B83A14273' temploid='98D38EEECE444e19ABF3CCD66F039F8B' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Request CAN-ID</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The request CAN identifier for functional requests.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.ReqCanIdFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDABC0' oid='ACA87035686A413fAA596301CE9BB261' temploid='D7C6DBD75AB2428999CB3D6478EFBC73' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='150' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a request message for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.P2Client</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDAD70' oid='31E5FED11F8E439f890E80F088912F34' temploid='E588673E14E74b65ADE1773EE2B0C5B0' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the reception of a request message. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.The tester will also require the P2Server timeout, since in UDS service "DiagnosticSessionControl"returns the P2Server and P2*Server timeouts – the tester has to calculate the offset manually and has to add it to the returned P2Server and P2*Server timeouts.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.P2Server</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDAF20' oid='2CEEB0EFB986434fA6793CEB7C595FA5' temploid='6AB483631DA74e2bB22D840FBF6E9D03' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='2000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2*Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enhanced timeout for the client to wait after the reception of a negative response message with response code 78 hex for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.P2ExClient</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDB0D0' oid='F4528E1674FD437cA9C233BA3809230B' temploid='EB0FA702B71845969D4BF5443CBA5C44' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='1950' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2*Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the transmission of a negative response message with response code 78 hex (enhanced response timing). In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.P2ExServer</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDB280' oid='7BB0ACAB415444da94ADE638D92CCA52' temploid='4B4467C830304b02BE5F4F900B57A143' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='4000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time between functionally addressed Tester Present request messages transmitted by the client to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active in multiple servers (functional communication) or maximum time between physically transmitted request messages to a single server (physical communication).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.S3Client</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CDB430' oid='D20D4A963EFC4c42B488232FDA9E82F5' temploid='59E3F213532C4e1a91342063BAAC2ABA' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for the server to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active while not receiving any diagnostic request message</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.S3Server</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE4A20' oid='891F3B32B66441908E941BBCB56F42E5' temploid='17DD456E67EF4e61A687CE827A707512' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a physically addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) with no response required before it can transmit the next physically addressed request message.
Minimum value = P2Server</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.P3ClientPhys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE4BD0' oid='CD49502AEED54509857ABA3C65624FE3' temploid='E2ECD88B055B47d5AAF5E03989C9303B' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='15872' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterPresentPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the TesterPresent message for physically addressed requests used to keep a diagnostic session active.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TesterPresentPhys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE4D80' oid='8A2D8DC999B44c5a94199A859C7DB4ED' temploid='1BAD0541DD8B43e8A099AD60D5D98A3C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a functionally addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) before it can transmit the next functionally addressed request message in case no response is required or the requested data is only supported by a subset of the functionally addressed servers.
Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.P3ClientFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE4F30' oid='487274D0F27E4b3cBB34DBF21F923B7F' temploid='036E136390AA484bB1607C71C37F05C3' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='16000' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterPresentFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the TesterPresent message for functionally addressed requests used to keep a diagnostic session active.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TesterPresentFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE50E0' oid='83CE1A5C155F4b30946E12443E45F16A' temploid='0107648AF7CE43eaA23F2B5F63162ABB' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='20' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>STmin</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(Separation Time) defines the minimum time gap between consecutive frames.Values from 0x00 to 0x7F (0 – 127) are absolute milliseconds.Values from 0xF1 to 0xF9 are even 100 micro seconds.Every other value range is reserved and should not be used.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.StMin</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE5290' oid='C4900AFA57F34392917F3686399999FA' temploid='F4068E95653F4a38A9B6FACFA5C00C94' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Blocksize</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The Blocksize parameter indicates, how many consecutive frames shall be sent in a transmission before a flow control frame is sent. The number 0 tells the sender, that no more flow controls should disrupt the sending of the remaining flow controls</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.Blocksize</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE5440' oid='48BFFB5807E94bfaA19373B395A519F9' temploid='DD3B57703DE4434099B0F4CB47352FBC' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout As</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for transmission of frame, sender side</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TimeoutAs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE55F0' oid='B9339DE0E6FD4e399C95CDB1C35CA566' temploid='10DFA8BAF1E042248A121E1CDE1FE07C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Ar</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for transmission of frame, receiver side</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TimeoutAr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CE57A0' oid='EF4B110FFDDE47a68F57D9131EDEF5FC' temploid='0BEFE1B7B67946b28BB870E654E603C0' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Bs</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until reception of next flow control</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TimeoutBs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEBA20' oid='63574CBAF9B64ebc99429189ADEADCC5' temploid='9CF20D5FEC4B45d9AE0E8F54396962CD' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time Br</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for next transmission of flow control</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TimeBr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEBBD0' oid='D82BD866722F418e80F37596B4F1ECD4' temploid='E2A2804DF25547979C447BC924425B97' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time Cs</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until next transmission of consecutive frame</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TimeCs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEBD80' oid='467C02197DF44753873E1D2164F5A4A7' temploid='0A4314F620E84facB52898C1F4683A21' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Cr</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until reception of next consecutive frame</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.TimeoutCr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEBF30' oid='8D700C63B766454b98DD59D8BF48B5CB' temploid='C0C91B8B8CB34b8f9B30D89D249F357C' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='4095' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Max Length of TP Message</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.MaxLengthTpMessage</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEC0E0' oid='AFA0F69497794e83B1BEF193B16663D7' temploid='8FC68D4BE54F435990B6F7A557105E45' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='500000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Baudrate</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Bus Speed of the used transport media. Caution, the Bus Speed has to be set identical in all ECUs connected to one subnet.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.Baudrate</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEC290' oid='8B52C0976B5C48d49F1C7996659C65EF' temploid='C66A73F1E7734ab19B0B5AFD7C746E33' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CANFrameFillerByte</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Fill byte used for filling CAN frames to eight byte length.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.CANFrameFillerByte</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE3850' oid='0848933E36534c729E37F60F8BC8CD06' temploid='2E724EEE20344fc3BF7B8E41AAD3C814' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>FillerByteHandling</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enables use of fill bytes; if "true", fill bytes are used, otherwise DLC may be smaller than 8.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_11Bit.FillerByteHandling</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>false</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>true</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE39F0' oid='44C8D7AA579C4ef394EB698277A86032' temploid='8EE526DF34114b55BB6DAD591866AE0D' attrcatref='_00000000053B6660' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Normal J1939</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE3B90' oid='3CD68D9E53894cfd90886279B9B3104D' temploid='54CFB623522141a390E8E4B9C003D4F7' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Bus Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Type of transport media</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.BusType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE3D30' oid='5D18B365CB3845ff9631B52BC65CDC70' temploid='9C9A40BEFD3A458fBD981F02A133B2A0' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Transport Protocol Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Type of used Transport Protocol (e.g. ISO15765)</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TransportProtocolType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>ISO15765</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE3ED0' oid='3FD3CD0722B141bbA902FE8E9AEF4E26' temploid='24EAAC4BADA242a79B7EB6B54B7EBADE' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for physical requests and responses.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.AddrScheme</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Normal</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='3'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE4070' oid='EF398FE52C1E41558283D0957036B141' temploid='20AE2F8A72694670974AF1B123C20D92' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='2' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for physical requests and responses</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.CanIdType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='2'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>J1939</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEC440' oid='6106AF7C536845b2890F920F3C188E3F' temploid='0A91A23F615D48ddB51AA9B988498F6C' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>ECU Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Physical diagnostic address of the ECU.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.EcuAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEC5F0' oid='1840AB6CA5FC40cdA37A9003FEA180AB' temploid='88917CF968524626AED122102BC90454' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='241' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Default Tester Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Usind this Addressing Scheme the ECU can determine the Tester Address required for the response direction from the received request. Therefore only a default Tester Address is required.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.DefaultTesterAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEC7A0' oid='A1196F9B1D474171A88F9106E1ADD9BC' temploid='EB86FDC7C00343a19640F6C3D25F08B7' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='6' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Default Tx-Priority</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The priority is user defined with a default value of six (6). The three bits priority field is used to optimize message latency for transmission onto the CAN bus only. The priority field should be masked off by the receiver (ignored). The priority of any CAN message can be set from highest, 0 (000 bin), to lowest, 7 (111 bin).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.DefaultTxPriority</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CEC950' oid='11624B9CD54A414790550FBB2F3645B7' temploid='D841FCA6E679492eBD40BC37CBE54833' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address Extension</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address Extension transmitted with the first data byte of the message frame. The Address Extension usually specifies a different subnet.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.AddressExtension</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE4210' oid='004B180BD01B4c209CAD5281FDC4263B' temploid='F28950B1087948478CD6D88B4EB8E698' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for functional requests.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.AddrSchemeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Normal</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='3'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020CE43B0' oid='301D38E8EB424d3c9FF1739FDA53D277' temploid='26612EECC3074b15B3DA2539F0C12DD6' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='2' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for functional request</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.CanIdTypeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='2'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>J1939</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CECB00' oid='AEEA91F7EFCD48838DE59C7B14390ADC' temploid='9E697990E3EE4557AB1EADB4BB9E9790' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='2' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Broadcast Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address of the functional group the ECU belongs to.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.BroadcastAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CECCB0' oid='DBBE6756AC0946e9B4D0294283D4FB75' temploid='03AB56B956664f839DC1BF917EB65BA3' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='150' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a request message for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.P2Client</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CECE60' oid='598D930B7C054f978BECCEF37BDAA2EC' temploid='0FD297B2B47E4788B37C77A4386072F1' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the reception of a request message. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.The tester will also require the P2Server timeout, since in UDS service "DiagnosticSessionControl"returns the P2Server and P2*Server timeouts – the tester has to calculate the offset manually and has to add it to the returned P2Server and P2*Server timeouts.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.P2Server</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CED010' oid='2E07A5F8B9D84ce6B62ABE8E19F00C12' temploid='CE9E1AD7D1654eafBC814ACD26EC5DD4' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='2000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2*Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enhanced timeout for the client to wait after the reception of a negative response message with response code 78 hex for the start of incoming response messages. In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.P2ExClient</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CED1C0' oid='3D5A6F709DE2432288A4A686EFD86904' temploid='2A64142437A840f6995B56885AE6DC25' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='1950' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P2*Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Performance requirement for the server to start with the response message after the transmission of a negative response message with response code 78 hex (enhanced response timing). In UDS this is the timeout for the default session.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.P2ExServer</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CED370' oid='13FA6AE859C242bc99772692D935F3FE' temploid='2B3C7EE3B9254e4898B211FC97C47011' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='4000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Client</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time between functionally addressed Tester Present request messages transmitted by the client to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active in multiple servers (functional communication) or maximum time between physically transmitted request messages to a single server (physical communication).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.S3Client</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CED520' oid='15118B4EEF8347c0A0EE7E379410E643' temploid='B68857B0277D40cbBDA06FFBBDFE1A02' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='5000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>S3Server</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for the server to keep a diagnostic session other than the defaultSession active while not receiving any diagnostic request message</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.S3Server</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CED6D0' oid='B60645810D8C4bde9F7156C0E189ECA8' temploid='1BA19EAE6D3B462c97CAEC2F74E75130' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a physically addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) with no response required before it can transmit the next physically addressed request message.
Minimum value = P2Server</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.P3ClientPhys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CF96F0' oid='5784090E9A754c3f84C8A3245E066A88' temploid='76FB35F264524633976FA2A6293862C8' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='15872' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterPresentPhys</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the TesterPresent message for physically addressed requests used to keep a diagnostic session active.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TesterPresentPhys</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CF98A0' oid='ECF70EF2CF0242b8832AD6A42838F009' temploid='48450C5A87C04e1694C5B2B3A6BD07AD' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>P3ClientFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Minimum time for the client to wait after the successful transmission of a functionally addressed request message (indicated via N_USData.con) before it can transmit the next functionally addressed request message in case no response is required or the requested data is only supported by a subset of the functionally addressed servers.
Minimum value = P2Server.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.P3ClientFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CF9A50' oid='27E9EB2E97934157834E3953A79D336E' temploid='0849203C81CD4e76A76926E72C89A467' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='16000' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>TesterPresentFunc</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Defines the TesterPresent message for functionally addressed requests used to keep a diagnostic session active.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TesterPresentFunc</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CF9C00' oid='600B565BADCF4d468077D21CC7BD41FB' temploid='6F9380EE3C44466bAE2378560CA18102' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='20' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>STmin</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>(Separation Time) defines the minimum time gap between consecutive frames.Values from 0x00 to 0x7F (0 – 127) are absolute milliseconds.Values from 0xF1 to 0xF9 are even 100 micro seconds.Every other value range is reserved and should not be used.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.StMin</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CF9DB0' oid='CF156DCDD2CB47d79683E04384A5F481' temploid='4177188CF9CB40479E16AD402453DEF6' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Blocksize</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The Blocksize parameter indicates, how many consecutive frames shall be sent in a transmission before a flow control frame is sent. The number 0 tells the sender, that no more flow controls should disrupt the sending of the remaining flow controls</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.Blocksize</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CF9F60' oid='6476B3BE546C47899A426EFD422FE439' temploid='F5A56E8AAB724bf98828E9C520151271' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout As</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for transmission of frame, sender side</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TimeoutAs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFA110' oid='830A1B55D8404a11930406C4E276636C' temploid='387DEF6532B546eaA2E1E35D781BE75C' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Ar</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for transmission of frame, receiver side</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TimeoutAr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFA2C0' oid='47FF4F056FB44a3aA1DFABFE9CC9CED2' temploid='851CD20C9AAE4dcb9816BC3ADBA1D2EF' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Bs</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until reception of next flow control</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TimeoutBs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFA470' oid='578047AB23BA46d488016EF50A10C86A' temploid='C35B9F3D7D334874805971D3652FB617' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time Br</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time for next transmission of flow control</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TimeBr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFAAF0' oid='AD8B33A9478A427e8A8CF0473DFCF081' temploid='E7CB66A53ED04d5e98AB32C4F814C4EF' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time Cs</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until next transmission of consecutive frame</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TimeCs</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFACA0' oid='D33AA12D26C34cf392B4C82E47616BA0' temploid='2B74FEE928714b95BD1E607570AA2A19' attrcatref='_00000000053B6A50' usage='sys' v='100' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Timeout Cr</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Time until reception of next consecutive frame</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.TimeoutCr</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFAE50' oid='21F778368F984fa5AF8DB6B5FC04FD0E' temploid='601A223D706847b3AE41C3AAE0A8B095' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='4095' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Max Length of TP Message</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.MaxLengthTpMessage</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFB000' oid='BE06E359A375459a9735D928ECE7C6A5' temploid='B6BF3A11F66D460d986463A0F8BD8C1F' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='500000' df='dec'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Baudrate</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Bus Speed of the used transport media. Caution, the Bus Speed has to be set identical in all ECUs connected to one subnet.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.Baudrate</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFB1B0' oid='42FE1F06392D4b0294BCBD6734CE40C5' temploid='79B51A381BD54f3680C60B09770813F6' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CANFrameFillerByte</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Fill byte used for filling CAN frames to eight byte length.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.CANFrameFillerByte</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D05AF0' oid='F039A134E2B340d5AE04E46E48FD5F45' temploid='9BCEAF20FD2440ccA5BDCC21A96FC2E9' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>FillerByteHandling</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Enables use of fill bytes; if "true", fill bytes are used, otherwise DLC may be smaller than 8.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Normal_J1939.FillerByteHandling</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>false</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>true</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D05C90' oid='BA08AD285184477cA92B9210E42BFE8B' temploid='7FD1F7E9AF554be8AEF48B04BD9B5739' attrcatref='_00000000053B6660' usage='sys' v='1' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed J1939</TUV>
</NAME>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>not supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='1'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>supported</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D05E30' oid='BD28512CDC694702A12835C4599292E6' temploid='9015741F62504045BF737AB86277FA22' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Bus Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Type of transport media</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.BusType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D05FD0' oid='D304AF81DB5D434e8F87716A2F0C1BCD' temploid='6FC1496D5B1B4855B9A16DD52980DDD5' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Transport Protocol Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Type of used Transport Protocol (e.g. ISO15765)</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.TransportProtocolType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>ISO15765</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D06170' oid='E1DFAC3396D04389B8131105CB927DCA' temploid='4D3AEDDACFDF4d19862757C41E5B33C1' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='3' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for physical requests and responses.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.AddrScheme</QUAL>
<ETAG v='3'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D06310' oid='85EF2B6F1FCB42e58AA9984A60079A68' temploid='3D8AF3B0223B4ccf90DAD761B62238B6' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='2' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>CAN-ID Type used for physical requests and responses</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.CanIdType</QUAL>
<ETAG v='0'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>11-Bit</TUV>
</ETAG>
<ETAG v='2'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>J1939</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFB360' oid='86A7D542BE2145dfA222EDD9C3CF4277' temploid='33BDC37369FC43948234BED763009738' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='1' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>ECU Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Physical diagnostic address of the ECU.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.EcuAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFB510' oid='B9E7DF08C0164faaA1E0C1C348F3D765' temploid='AE365BAE13EB4e6a80E0A23AF29F7B40' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='241' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Default Tester Address</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Usind this Addressing Scheme the ECU can determine the Tester Address required for the response direction from the received request. Therefore only a default Tester Address is required.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.DefaultTesterAddress</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFB6C0' oid='75085AD7DE79491aBACACF811CC46704' temploid='C4622FDB85804705AA0968F700E87A80' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='6' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Default Tx-Priority</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The priority is user defined with a default value of six (6). The three bits priority field is used to optimize message latency for transmission onto the CAN bus only. The priority field should be masked off by the receiver (ignored). The priority of any CAN message can be set from highest, 0 (000 bin), to lowest, 7 (111 bin).</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.DefaultTxPriority</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<UNSDEF id='_0000000020CFB870' oid='49F855D50F3041c394C2AA1B86DD2BED' temploid='5AB6BA73715C45499BFD509BDDA8F459' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='0' df='hex'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address Extension</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Address Extension transmitted with the first data byte of the message frame. The Address Extension usually specifies a different subnet.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.AddressExtension</QUAL>
</UNSDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D064B0' oid='85FDE264164E44cfB2AEBF4400760A77' temploid='AFB137FA7C06405a970A5F2D4330EE82' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='3' sort='id'>
<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Functional Addressing Scheme</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Addressing Scheme used for functional requests.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>Mixed_J1939.AddrSchemeFunc</QUAL>
<ETAG v='3'>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Mixed</TUV>
</ETAG>
</ENUMDEF>
<ENUMDEF id='_0000000020D06650' oid='E7D1D35592A948e1A993B8F0BC53FB91' temploid='BFE4F1AA4DEB4a8aA3365F541F849AC3' attrcatref='_00000000053B63C0' usage='sys' v='2' sort='id'>
<NAME>
