<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Security Access Type</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The sub-function parameter securityAccessType indicates to the server the step in progress for this service, the level of security the client wants to access and the format of seed and key. If a server supports different levels of security each level shall be identified by the requestSeed value, which has a fixed relationship to the sendKey value.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>securityAccessType</QUAL>
</DATAOBJ>
</SIMPLECOMPCONT>
<SIMPLECOMPCONT oid='8DD43A9BB9834942A6CDB4F46B936E02' temploid='60C15282D924439cA356B60388FBA9EB' shproxyref='_0000000020E65310'>
