<NAME>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>Security Seed</TUV>
</NAME>
<DESC>
<TUV xml:lang='en-US'>The seed parameter is a data value sent by the server and is used by the client when calculating the key needed to access security. The securitySeed data bytes are only present in the response message if the request message was sent with the sub-function set to a value which requests the seed of the server.</TUV>
</DESC>
<QUAL>securitySeed</QUAL>
</DATAOBJ>
</SIMPLECOMPCONT>
